-- The Monitoring Worker Agents.
--
-- Sixty agents whose whole job is to look and say. They extend the same
-- register the twenty operational agents use - public.ai_agents - so there is
-- one roster, one permission constraint and one audit table rather than a
-- second workforce beside the first.
--
-- Every one of them is granted exactly READ, ANALYZE, RECOMMEND and CREATE.
-- CREATE is what lets them file an alert or a report; it does not let them
-- change anything they are watching. None is granted EXECUTE_LOW_RISK,
-- because the rule is that only an explicitly authorized low-risk action may
-- execute, and none has been authorized. APPROVE cannot be granted to any of
-- them: the constraint on ai_agents does not admit the verb at all, which is
-- also why no monitoring agent can be made to change permissions, alter
-- security, touch code or git, deploy, or repair infrastructure.
--
-- The Developer Monitoring Agent is the one worth naming twice. It watches
-- development health through read-only signals, and the same constraint that
-- governs the rest is what stops it from ever becoming a development agent.
--
-- All sixty are registered CONFIGURED. None has been assigned work, none has
-- a run, and runs_30d and success_rate keep their zero defaults, because zero
-- is the truth.

ON CONFLICT (agent_key) WHERE agent_key IS NOT NULL DO UPDATE SET
  name           = EXCLUDED.name,
  purpose        = EXCLUDED.purpose,
  specialization = EXCLUDED.specialization,
  capability     = EXCLUDED.capability,
  permissions    = EXCLUDED.permissions,
  system_prompt  = EXCLUDED.system_prompt;
